### BOMS - OData V4 CRUD test collection
###
### Every URL and payload below was verified against a running instance.
###
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client, already
### recommended in .vscode/extensions.json) and imports into Postman as well.
###
### Start the app first:   npm start        -> http://localhost:4004
### After deploying to BTP, point @host at your route:
###   https://<route>.cfapps.<region>.hana.ondemand.com
###
### URL contract notes (learned the hard way, so you do not have to):
###   * The service is mounted at /boms, so the base path is /boms, NOT
###     /odata/v4/boms.
###   * Associations are addressed by a nested object or by the foreign key
###     column, never by a bare key string:
###       WRONG   { "requestedBy": "e1000000-..." }
###       RIGHT   { "requestedBy": { "employeeId": "e1000000-..." } }
###       ALSO OK { "requestedBy_employeeId": "e1000000-..." }
###   * EmployeeProjects has a composite key of the two foreign key columns.
###   * Navigation follows the association as declared, so
###     /ServiceRequests(<id>)/requestedBy works, while
###     /Employees(<id>)/requestedBy does not exist.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@base = {{host}}/boms
@json = application/json


### ===========================================================================
### 1. SERVICE DOCUMENT / METADATA
### ===========================================================================

### Service document. Lists the 10 BOMS entity sets.
GET {{base}}/

### OData V4 metadata document: keys, associations, enum code lists.
GET {{base}}/$metadata


### ===========================================================================
### 2. READ - all 10 entities (2 sample records each)
### ===========================================================================

GET {{base}}/Departments
###
GET {{base}}/Employees
###
GET {{base}}/Projects
###
GET {{base}}/EmployeeProjects
###
GET {{base}}/ServiceRequests
###
GET {{base}}/RequestApprovals
###
GET {{base}}/RequestComments
###
GET {{base}}/RequestHistories
###
GET {{base}}/KnowledgeCategories
###
GET {{base}}/KnowledgeArticles


### ===========================================================================
### 3. READ - filter, order, select, expand, navigate
### ===========================================================================

### Critical and high priority requests, most severe first
GET {{base}}/ServiceRequests?$filter=priority le 2&$orderby=priority asc&$select=title,priority,status

### Requests in a given status
GET {{base}}/ServiceRequests?$filter=status eq 'InProgress'

### Only published articles
GET {{base}}/KnowledgeArticles?$filter=status eq 'Published'

### One employee, expanded along both associations
GET {{base}}/Employees(e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001)?$expand=department,manager

### One request, expanded to requester, assignee and department at once
GET {{base}}/ServiceRequests(r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001)?$expand=requestedBy,assignedTo,department

### Navigate along an association: request -> the employee that raised it
GET {{base}}/ServiceRequests(r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001)/requestedBy

### Approvals of one request. The association is declared on RequestApprovals,
### so the parent has no inverse navigation property - filter on the child
### instead of navigating upwards. Note the quoted GUID: OData needs string
### literals quoted, also for Edm.Guid values.
GET {{base}}/RequestApprovals?$filter=request/requestId eq 'r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'

### The same request traversed from the other side
GET {{base}}/RequestComments?$filter=request/requestId eq 'r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'&$expand=request,commentedBy

### One project allocation, addressed by its composite key
GET {{base}}/EmployeeProjects(employee_employeeId=e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001,project_projectId=p1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001)

### Count only
GET {{base}}/ServiceRequests/$count

### First 2, sorted
GET {{base}}/ServiceRequests?$top=2&$orderby=priority asc

### Text search on article content, the field a RAG pipeline indexes
GET {{base}}/KnowledgeArticles?$filter=contains(content,'certificate')&$select=title,status


### ===========================================================================
### 4. CREATE - POST
### ===========================================================================

### Keys are UUIDs that CAP fills in automatically, and the managed fields
### (createdAt, createdBy, modifiedAt, modifiedBy) are set by the server.
# @name createDepartment
POST {{base}}/Departments
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "departmentName": "Finance",
  "description": "Budgeting, invoicing and financial reporting."
}

### Create a knowledge category
POST {{base}}/KnowledgeCategories
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "categoryName": "Security & Compliance",
  "description": "Data protection, audit and policy topics."
}

### Create a service request. Associations go in as nested objects.
POST {{base}}/ServiceRequests
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "title": "Laptop will not boot after update",
  "description": "Device stays on the company logo screen after the nightly patch.",
  "requestType": "Incident",
  "priority": 2,
  "requestedBy": { "employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002" },
  "assignedTo": { "employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "department": { "departmentId": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "dueDate": "2026-03-01T17:00:00Z"
}

### Create a knowledge article. `content` is what a RAG pipeline chunks and
### embeds, so this is the most interesting one to POST.
POST {{base}}/KnowledgeArticles
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "title": "How to request a new laptop",
  "content": "Submit a request through the self service portal. The IT Operations team assesses it within two working days and assigns a loan device in the meantime.",
  "category": { "categoryId": "k1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "author": { "employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "status": "Draft"
}

### Create an approval on the second sample request
POST {{base}}/RequestApprovals
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "request": { "requestId": "r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002" },
  "approver": { "employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "approvalStatus": "Pending",
  "comments": "Checking with the data protection officer."
}

### Add a comment to a request
POST {{base}}/RequestComments
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "request": { "requestId": "r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "commentedBy": { "employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "commentText": "Certificate reissued, users asked to reconnect."
}

### Employee-project allocation, composite key of both foreign keys
POST {{base}}/EmployeeProjects
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "employee": { "employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "project": { "projectId": "p1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002" },
  "projectRole": "Technical Lead"
}


### ===========================================================================
### 5. UPDATE - PATCH
### ===========================================================================

### Change status and assign an engineer. modifiedAt/modifiedBy are set by the
### server, you never send them.
PATCH {{base}}/ServiceRequests(r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "status": "Assigned",
  "assignedTo": { "employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" }
}

### The same update through the foreign key column
PATCH {{base}}/ServiceRequests(r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "assignedTo_employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"
}

### Approve a pending request
PATCH {{base}}/RequestApprovals(a1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "approvalStatus": "Approved",
  "approvedAt": "2026-02-04T09:00:00Z",
  "comments": "Approved, least privilege access granted."
}

### Publish a draft article
PATCH {{base}}/KnowledgeArticles(n1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "status": "Published",
  "publishedAt": "2026-02-05T09:00:00Z"
}

### Append to the audit trail
POST {{base}}/RequestHistories
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "request": { "requestId": "r1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002" },
  "action": "StatusChange",
  "oldStatus": "New",
  "newStatus": "Assigned",
  "performedBy": { "employeeId": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" },
  "comments": "Assigned to the IT Operations queue."
}


### ===========================================================================
### 6. DELETE
### ===========================================================================

### Expect 204 No Content.
DELETE {{base}}/RequestHistories(h1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)

### Expect 404, it is gone.
GET {{base}}/RequestHistories(h1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)

### Clean up the department created in section 4
DELETE {{base}}/Departments({{createDepartment.response.body.departmentId}})


### ===========================================================================
### 7. NEGATIVE TESTS - error handling
### ===========================================================================

### Unknown entity set - expect 404
GET {{base}}/DoesNotExist

### Key that does not exist - expect 404
GET {{base}}/ServiceRequests(00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000)

### Missing a mandatory field (departmentName is not null) - expect 400
POST {{base}}/Departments
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "description": "Missing the mandatory name."
}

### Value outside the enum vocabulary (priority only allows 1..4) - expect 400
POST {{base}}/ServiceRequests
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "title": "Invalid priority",
  "priority": 99
}

### Association given a bare key string instead of an object - expect 400
POST {{base}}/ServiceRequests
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "title": "Wrong association shape",
  "requestedBy": "e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"
}
